Scope of the Standard

Shunyaya Structural Alphabet Unification (SSAU) defines a deterministic structural governance layer for deterministic domains.

SSAU establishes:

Finite Structural Regime Space SRS(D)

Governance lattice boundedness

Injection stability

Collision stability

Replay-verifiable determinism

Preservation of classical measurable quantities

The governing invariant is:

phi((m,a,s)) = m

SSAU does not:

modify domain equations
introduce predictive models
unify physical forces
simulate system dynamics
guarantee safety outcomes

SSAU governs structural admissibility, not causation.


Conformance

An implementation conforms to the SSAU Open Standard if it:

Preserves classical measurement:

phi((m,a,s)) = m

Produces deterministic structural regime extraction.

Collapses regimes into a bounded governance lattice:
DENY <= ABSTAIN <= ALLOW_RESTRICTED <= ALLOW

Produces byte-identical artifacts under independent replay:

B_A = B_B

Remains bounded under deterministic injection.

Resolves cross-domain collision deterministically.

Any implementation introducing:

randomness
probabilistic inference
adaptive tuning
tolerance-based decision logic
nondeterministic output

does not conform to the SSAU Open Standard.

Independent implementations are permitted and encouraged.


